# Desktop UI

Follow skill `mangodisk-style-desktop-ui`.

**UI: match MangoDisk** — shell, density, soft surfaces, sidebar, workspaces, dialogs, light/dark.  
**Branding: PC Toolkit Pro only** — name, logo, primary accent, `pt-*` components. Never ship their name, mango logo, or GPL source.

## Hard rules

- Vue is presentation; side effects in `lib/services/`; workflow in Pinia stores.
- Semantic CSS tokens only. No random hex in pages.
- Shell: sidebar + page shell + (toolbar → results → action bar).
- Buttons: color/border/shadow only — never translate/scale.
- No raw SVG in templates — icon components only.
- Locales for all user-facing text.
- When layout choices conflict, prefer looking like MangoDisk over a custom redesign.
- Fast/no-hang: hidden window until mount; no startup scans; lazy secondary pages; long work off UI thread with progress + cancel.

## Result pages

- Fixed-height workspace toolbar.
- Dense result rows (~44px); medium weight primary text.
- Confirm before destructive clean/delete; show estimated reclaimable size.

## Prefer

```vue
<PtPageShell title="..." content-mode="workspace">
  <PtResultWorkspace>...</PtResultWorkspace>
</PtPageShell>
```
